payload.prompt:
Build a /tracker page for FibreFlow. This is a standalone page (like /conduit) with an editable PON table.

STEP 1 - Create pages/api/tracker/[projectId].ts:
```typescript
import type { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from "next";
import { apiResponse } from "@/lib/apiResponse";
export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  const { projectId } = req.query;
  if (req.method === "GET") {
    return res.status(200).json(apiResponse(true, "OK", { pons: [], projectId }));
  }
  if (req.method === "POST") {
    return res.status(200).json(apiResponse(true, "Saved", {}));
  }
  res.status(405).json(apiResponse(false, "Method not allowed"));
}
```

STEP 2 - Create src/modules/tracker/components/PonTrackerTable.tsx with these exact columns:
Zone No | HLD PON | Z-PON | OLT Port | Scope Poles | Scope Drops | Pole Permission (date) | Poles Planted | CWC Poles Date (date) | CWC Stringing Date (date) | Ready for Optical (date) | CWC QA (checkbox) | Optical Splicing (date) | Optical Submitted (date) | Optical Activated (date) | ATP QA (checkbox) | Sign-ups | Homes PO | Homes Recon | Activated | Available | Blockage (text)

Interface for a row:
```typescript
interface PonRow {
  id: string;
  zone_no: number | null;
  hld_pon: number | null;
  z_pon: number | null;
  olt_port: string;
  scope_poles: number | null;
  scope_drops: number | null;
  pole_permission: string;
  poles_planted: number | null;
  cwc_poles_date: string;
  cwc_stringing_date: string;
  ready_for_optical: string;
  cwc_qa: boolean;
  optical_splicing_date: string;
  optical_submitted_date: string;
  optical_activated_date: string;
  atp_qa: boolean;
  sign_ups: number | null;
  homes_po: number | null;
  homes_recon: number | null;
  activated: number | null;
  available: number | null;
  blockage: string;
}
```

Props: `{ rows: PonRow[], editMode: boolean, onChange: (rows: PonRow[]) => void }`
- In read mode: show values as plain text
- In edit mode: show inputs (type="number", type="date", type="checkbox", type="text")
- Sticky header row
- Totals row at bottom (sum numeric columns)
- Row with blockage text: highlight with amber left border
- Horizontal scroll for wide table

STEP 3 - Create src/modules/tracker/components/PonTrackerPage.tsx:
- Props: `{ projectId: string }`
- State: rows, editMode, loading, saving
- Fetch GET /api/tracker/${projectId} on mount
- "Edit" button → enables editMode
- "Add Row" button (in edit mode) → appends blank row with crypto.randomUUID()
- "Save" button → POST /api/tracker/${projectId} with rows, then exit editMode
- "Discard" button → revert to last saved state
- Render PonTrackerTable
- Show "X rows · Last saved: never" below header

STEP 4 - Create pages/tracker.tsx:
- Fetch projects list from /api/projects?limit=50
- Project selector dropdown at top (show project name)
- Default to first project
- Render PonTrackerPage with selected projectId
- Use same page layout as other FF pages (look at pages/conduit.tsx for the layout pattern)
- Title: "PON Tracker"

STEP 5 - Add to sidebar:
Find where nav items are defined (search for "Conduit" in src/ to find the nav config).
Add entry: { label: "PON Tracker", href: "/tracker", icon: <TableIcon or similar> }
Place it after "Conduit" in the nav.

After writing all files, run: npm run type-check 2>&1 | tail -30

When done: openclaw system event --text "Done: /tracker page with editable PON table complete" --mode now
